"""Publish dimensioned, source-linked construction contracts for the generated place."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,xml.etree.ElementTree as ET
from world_spec import records
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
DETAILS={
 'tetris':'10 columns × 6 Studs; block cell 6×6×24; 20 logical rows. Seven canonical tetrominoes rotate in the X/Y plane. Fall at 2.2 rows/s, fast drop 14 rows/s, difficulty scales speed. Locking stores each cell separately. Full rows are removed and every cell above is lowered by the number of cleared rows. One curator at a physical console; three survivor spawn points. Next-shape selection has seven physical buttons. A curator wins only if no survivor qualifies; otherwise survivors compete by survival and line-key points.',
 'maze':'9×9 connected graph, 12 Stud cell spacing, 1×14 walls. Depth-first spanning-tree construction guarantees connectivity. Replanning every 1.2s uses breadth-first paths across open edges. Hunter detection radius 70; outside detection it patrols graph nodes. Its articulated jaw follows its carriage. Collect at least three pellets and remain alive to qualify.',
 'duel':'Opposed floors at X=-38/+38; bridges at Y=0/24/48. Server creates an actual metal sword Tool. Attack reach 9, facing-dot threshold 0.15, damage 34, recovery 0.7s. F / screen strike is an additional input route. Server arm poses animate a swing. Surviving competitors are ranked by damage-related score and the central standard.',
 'chess':'8×8 board at 10 Stud square spacing; 32 physical pieces. Rook and bishop moves stop at occupied squares; queen combines both, knight jumps, king moves one square, pawn advances or captures diagonally and promotes. Sides alternate. A destination warning precedes a 1.3s animated move; collision during transit causes elimination. This is a chess-hazard survival trial, not a full checkmate/castling chess client.',
 'snake':'18 articulated segment bodies follow sampled head-position history at 5.5 Stud spacing, not independent animation loops. The head chooses legal neighboring nodes on a 32-node spatial route; four junctions offer alternate chords. Route height varies up to 15 Studs and neighboring samples interpolate continuously. Segments are oriented toward the preceding path sample. Raised refuge signals award points; contact starts a pressure death. Collect at least one signal and remain alive.',
 'bridge':'12 deck sections of 26×2×9.7 plus protected abutments. Section i warns/fades after i×4 seconds and loses support 1.4s later. The raft beneath is removed. Every player who reaches the far seal is recorded independently; crossing is mandatory for victory.',
 'lift':'30×2×30 carriage rides four guide rails; sinusoidal travel reaches Y=72. Standing characters are carried by the platform delta. Upper seal at Y=78 is required for victory; surrounding spiral landings provide alternate routes. The lobby/museum lift is a separate callable infrastructure system.',
 'rotatingmaze':'Three drum radii: 14/28/42. Each has ten wall sectors, leaving radial openings. Adjacent rings rotate in opposite directions at 0.14 rad/s. Rotated-box overlap detects pressure damage. The outer seal is required to qualify.',
 'rhythm':'6×6 numbered pads. Every 3.5s one safe pad is selected; the final 1.3s discharges all other occupied pads. Damage is time-integrated at 90 health/s, rather than a disconnected touch-kill. Organ pipes provide a physical silhouette; audible numbered musical cues require imported score IDs.',
 'frozen':'Ice partitions and four heat stations. Per-player heat starts at 15s, drains away from warmth, regenerates at 4/s within 12 Studs of a station. Zero heat starts freezing choreography. Ice material is used physically; this implementation does not yet include a separate friction/temperature body simulation.',
 'volcano':'Three visible vent boxes around a 25-Stud radius. One active vent per 5s phase; the first 2s warn, the remaining phase raises its harmful plume to 28 Studs. Contact burns. Obsidian seals are ordinary server-validated collectible objectives.',
 'domino':'16 separate 10×24×2 slabs. Slab i begins rotation at i×2s; rotation is computed around its lower hinge over 1.8s. The moving oriented face can crush characters. The final collection seal is placed beyond the chain.',
 'memory':'36 cells. Safe cells are illuminated; after 1.5s illumination is removed, and the final 1.3s of a 6s cycle discharges unsafe occupied cells. At least one safe cell is guaranteed. Memory differs from rhythm by multiple safe cells and a hidden projection phase.',
 'tower':'Connected spiral landings climb to roughly 71 Studs. Main floors at Y=0/22/44/66 are removed in sequence every 16s. Upper seal at Y=75 is required; waiting on the ground cannot win. Structural removal is scripted, not a whole-building unanchored collapse simulation.',
 'rotor':'Two long driven arms rotate at 0.35 rad/s around a visible drive shaft. Arm contact deals time-integrated pressure damage. Jumping avoids the low rotating sweep. Collecting exposed keys improves ranking.',
 'curatormaze':'Uses the connected graph engine but adds eight curator-operated shortcut gates. Opening disables wall collision and adds graph edges; closing restores collision and removes those edges. Base spanning-tree routes remain connected. The hunter replans after a switch and never routes through a closed gate.',
 'clock':'Minute arm speed 0.2 rad/s; hour arm speed one twelfth of minute speed. Arm lengths differ. A bell-refuge exit seal is enabled only after 70% of the round. Reaching it and remaining alive is required for victory.',
 'pendulum':'Five independently phased bobs. Pivots at Y=48, suspension length 42; angle sin(0.8t+phase)×0.9. Rod position and rotation are derived from the same pendulum angle. Swept bob contact triggers an impact death.',
 'balance':'Two pans at X=-24/+24. Team occupancy determines vertical pan offsets, 3 Studs per player imbalance. Equal nonzero load held for eight seconds completes the trial. All qualified surviving teammates receive trophies, not one random teammate.',
 'teamescape':'Four stations around a 32-Stud radius. Valve activations must overlap within a 12s window and come from min(4, participant count) distinct players. Each station has server proximity and 3s activation recovery. Team completion rewards every qualified survivor.',
 'walls':'Four rail-driven wall panels oscillate laterally at 0.35 rad/s with phase offsets. Hydraulic drive housings and floor rails mark their paths. Oriented overlap deals compression damage. No damage is emitted outside the moving panels.',
 'pinball':'7-Stud steel sphere with a 2D velocity state. It reflects at table bounds and rebounds radially from five bumpers. Player collision causes staged impact death. This deterministic kinematic table does not use Roblox unanchored ball physics.',
 'rooms':'Nine 30-Stud freight-room floors, with three wall partitions each. Rooms move on parallel rails in alternating directions each 7s cycle, carrying standing players and their partitions. The indicated room is safe during discharge; the final safe room is mandatory for qualification.',
 'gravity':'An explicitly magnetic trial, not a global Workspace.Gravity change. Every 12s, an 8–10s upward pulse adds vertical velocity; players must land on raised platforms and avoid the energized ceiling grid. Global gravity remains 196.2 for other simultaneous matches.',
 'drawbridge':'Twelve deck sections form two bascule leaves. Height and pitch derive from the same sinusoidal opening angle; passengers are carried by position delta. The far extraction seal is required. Runtime uses anchored leaf motion rather than constraint-driven counterweights.',
 'execution':'Six guided vertical rams in three lanes. A 7s machine cycle provides four seconds open, a one-second downstroke, then retraction; lanes are phase shifted by 0.7s. Actual ram overlap triggers the compression sequence.',
 'wheel':'Ten gondolas circulate on a radius-40 vertical wheel, centered at Y=44, speed 0.12 rad/s. Passengers are carried by delta; upper seal at Y=87 is mandatory. Gondolas remain level, as suspended cabins should.',
 'flood':'Atrium flood surface oscillates around Y=24 with amplitude 8. Each player has 12s underwater air and regenerates air at twice real time above the surface. Drowning is based on actual character elevation relative to the visible surface.',
 'risingwater':'Surface rises at 0.85 Stud/s from Y=-5. Forty-two connected landings provide an ascent route. Air lasts 12s underwater. The final seal at Y=75 must be reached; simply avoiding one wave does not qualify.',
 'corridors':'The connected 9×9 transit topology has twelve rail-guided shortcut shutters. Every 6s a different shortcut opens; its graph edge is added only after the physical panel clears the passage. Closed panels remove their graph edges and closing contact is lethal. Base tree connections remain intact, so there is always a valid route. There is no hunter in this trial. Three route seals and survival are required.',
 'furnace':'Mouth at Z=-42 opens on the latter part of a 9s cycle. Heat damage is applied outside baffle shelter and working cooling-station proximity. Cooling valves and exhaust infrastructure are physical objects. The current shelter test is geometric, not acoustic/thermal CFD.',
 'platforms':'64 isolated slabs. A selected index group becomes unsupported after a four-second visible warning window within an 8s group cycle. Structural raft is removed. Load is also tracked for visible stress coloration.',
 'press':'Six punch heads on physical guide posts. Seven-second stroke cycles are offset by 1.5s, creating crossing windows between banks. Position and harmful volume share the same moving object.',
 'debris':'Warnings at random locations, then masonry falls from Y=55 after 1.5s. Speed 45 Stud/s; position-overlap is checked at server tick intervals before debris passes below the floor. Each warning is removed with its own stone.',
 'gears':'Twelve short tooth bodies circulate at radius 31, speed 0.6 rad/s, around a fixed sun shaft. Their actual rotated volumes apply pressure damage. The exterior adds a visibly toothed gear crown.',
 'statues':'Five stone witnesses. Avatar facing direction, not an arbitrary global timer, determines whether any survivor is watching a statue. A watched statue stops; an unwatched statue pursues the nearest survivor at 10 Stud/s. Face with the avatar to stop it.',
 'shrink':'8×8 foundation district. Outer rows and columns detach every 18s by their minimum distance from the edge. The safe district contracts inward, while the visible failed tiles lose collision.',
 'crane':'Curator console targets trolley X and lowers a 14×12×14 cargo load. Hoist cable position and length derive from actual load height under an 80-Stud jib. With no curator, target motion is automated. Overlap with the suspended load triggers crushing.',
 'blades':'Five low rotating steel sweep bodies, phase shifted around a driven court. They deal time-integrated combat impact damage, not gore. The exterior supplies individual saw drives and axles; runtime blades are simplified bar cutters.',
 'collapse':'Each of 64 slabs integrates the time players stand on it. At 1.5s it shows stress; at 2.5s accumulated load it loses support. Different players contribute to the same slab load. Falling is handled by the connected fall choreography.',
 'shift':'Four rail carriages shuttle over a genuinely open trench; both the regular floor and raft are removed. Standing players follow the carriage delta. Protected docks sit at X=-44/+44. Far-dock extraction is required; falling triggers the fall animation and elimination. Rails remain visible beneath each carriage.',
 'bulkhead':'Three 20-Stud-high reinforced interlocks span the corridor at Z=-28/0/28. Collect physical lock teeth in sequence; a valid console grants an 8s opening. Paired leaves move apart at 0.6 opening units/s, exposing their rack drive. Closing leaf contact crushes. Side walls prevent walking around the mechanism. The final extraction seal is required; shared keys let the team advance together.',
 'machine':'Intake, compression and exhaust are explicit ordered stages. Three rotating intake cylinders pulse on an 8s cycle; the intake gives forward velocity. Three independently phased compression heads guard Z=0. A traversing exhaust shutter becomes harmful during the final part of a 10s phase. Per-player progress changes only on crossing Z=-20 then Z=22; the far seal at Z=55 requires stage three. Each physical moving mechanism supplies its own contact volume.',
 'pillars':'25 hydraulic columns. Independent sine phases raise each from Y=0 to Y=20 and retract it; passengers follow the position delta. Sockets and service distribution are visible. Collect elevated seals and stay on the columns.',
 'resonance':'Pressure rings spawn every 4s, expand at 10 Stud/s, and consist of 24 low glowing segments. Contact with a low ring deals shock damage; jumping clears the wave. Rings are destroyed after radius 60.',
 'mirrors':'A true geometric ray solver intersects oriented mirror boxes and opaque baffles. Up to six reflections use d′=d−2(d·n)n and stop at the nearest opaque obstruction or perimeter wall. The actual reflected path is rebuilt every 5s, shown transparently for 1.6s, then becomes harmful. Each visible beam segment uses the computed length and orientation. Mirror frames and baffles therefore affect gameplay, not only appearance.',
 'oxygen':'Four reservoirs rotate availability every 12s. Air reserve starts at 15s and recharges only within 12 Studs of the currently active reservoir; empty air causes suffocation choreography. Distinct from flood: elevation and water are irrelevant.',
 'switches':'Four relays must be activated in displayed cyclic order, eight correct activations total. Correct inputs score 30, wrong inputs damage by 25. Server range and per-station recovery are enforced. Eight correct relays are mandatory for victory.',
 'convoy':'Twelve freight beds span a long axis. A laterally oscillating loading gantry advances from Z=65 to -70 at 12 Stud/s and repeats. Contact causes impact death. Every player can record the far extraction seal.',
 'finale':'Three actual elevations (0/24/48) connect by two exterior stair flights with unobstructed slabs and landing bridges. First interlock opens after 25s; second after 50s. Middle stage runs a safe-cell memory projection, top stage activates a real rotating sweeper. Extraction at Y=52 is enabled only after 65s. The final seal and survival are mandatory; waiting on the ground cannot win.',
}
assert len(DETAILS)==50
root=ET.parse(ROOT/'Mountainverse.rbxlx').getroot()
counts={}
for m in root.iter('Item'):
 name=m.find("Properties/string[@name='Name']").text
 if name.startswith('Mountain') or name=='MuseumTemplate' or name=='Lobby': counts[name]=sum(1 for p in m.iter('Item') if p.attrib['class'] in ('Part','SpawnLocation'))
lines=['# MOUNTAINVERSE — construction and implementation ledger','',
'This document separates measured, generated objects from gameplay implemented in Luau and from requirements still outstanding. It is not a claim of a finished, Studio-tested release. All dimensions are Studs.','',
'## Common construction system','',
'`tools/architecture.py` creates the permanent map directly in XML. `src/Trials.lua` creates private trial interiors when a match starts; these are separate underground instances aligned with the mountain coordinates, not modifications of the public sightseeing structures. Reusable depth slots separate simultaneous teams. `src/Infrastructure.lua` binds real lift carriages and call buttons. Foundations, columns, floors, guideways, service galleries, lighting and signage are Parts with collision; glass has thickness and framing. Fine inscriptions, cable markers and light strips are visual details. Moving hazards are server-driven anchored Parts; contact uses their oriented boxes. This is a kinematic mechanism system, not a general rigid-body engineering simulator.','',
'## Central complex','',
'Foundation: 480 W × 12 H × 360 D, footprint 172,800. Open main plaza: 320×240 = 76,800. Meridian tower: 76×56 deck plates at 0/40/80/120/180/240, four 8-Stud structural piers, helical external stair with 480 treads (0.5 rise), roof lantern. Upper open decks add 21,280 of walkable area; these are not enclosed internal floors. Enclosed/roofed halls: two 62×300 navigation halls, market 120×36, service corridor 280×20, four 42×32 assembly bays; covered functional floor area 52,496, overlapping the ground circulation footprint rather than adding new land.','',
'Circulation design target: 32 simultaneous visitors, to be configured in Roblox experience settings. Even 32 people each using a 4×4 personal envelope occupy 512 square Studs; 40% of the main plaza alone reserves 30,720 for circulation. Arrival to northern assembly is roughly 240 Studs (15s at default walking speed). The lift provides a fast observation route; stairs provide an independent route. West: fifty engraved mountain stops. East: visitor directories for personal archives. South: market and arrival. North: four physical assembly halls.','',
'Lobby lift: four guide rails, cabin 12×1×12, upper/lower landings, hoist housing and cable. Both floors have call prompts. Smoothstep motion travels at an average scale of 14 Studs/s; each heartbeat carries standing characters by the cabin displacement. Stairs remain available if the lift is occupied.','',
'## Personal archives','',
'Each player receives a separate cloned architectural Model, not just a display room. Footprint: 360×320 = 115,200. Open courtyard: 200×160 = 32,000. Ground covered gallery floor: 83,200. Upper gallery after real stairwell openings and landings: 77,988. Total usable covered floor area: **161,188**. Floors at 0 and 32, roof at 65. Fifty plinths, twenty-five on each floor. Two 16-wide stair flights have actual slab openings; a two-stop lift gives an alternate route. Opposed galleries flank the pool; a 12-wide bridge crosses the court. Service walls, ducts, cabinets, perimeter columns, framed glazing and exhibit luminaires are generated.','',
'Each of the fifty exhibits has its own procedural architectural icon, scaled progressively with rank. Exhibits use stored victories, 20 material/color ranks and three mutation effects. Mud has particles and small positional animation. Museum directories in the east hall let visitors enter another player’s archive. A separate empty public archive is authored for edit-mode inspection. Live clones are placed on a 440-Stud pitch. Streaming is enabled (minimum radius 256, target 1024); lobby geometry persists, museums stream atomically, and noncolliding far silhouettes remain visible until full geometry is near. Teleports request their destination region. Museum idle animation runs only near visitors. Loading/replication performance still needs measurement in Studio.','',
'## Trial loop and common technical spaces','',
'Party admission → player-count check → private interior construction → 3s preparation → timed trial → 1.2s animation settlement → victory qualification and rewards → 4s return interval. A run contains five nonrepeating choices compatible with the party size. Admin solo inspection bypasses the minimum-player rule. Each private interior includes a reinforced raft unless the hazard needs an open pit, four load-bearing piers, overhead trusses, a service gallery, cable channel, technical annex, cabinet, ventilation trunk and work lights. Each public mountain has a 24×36 technical annex and a connected stair/service approach.','',
'Death is server-authoritative. Lethal contact starts recognition, defensive posture, resistance and loss-of-balance motor poses; only after roughly one second does health become zero and the score update. Freeze changes limb color; consume faces the jaw; impact and compression lean relative to the contact body. Cameras are never locked. These are shared procedural R6/R15 animations with cause-specific poses; there are **not fifty independently authored animation sets**.','',
'## Mountain contracts and current implementations','']
for g in records():
 key=f"Mountain{g['id']:02}_{g['kind']}"; fp=(g['width']+40)*(g['depth']+40)
 lines += [f"### {g['id']:02} — {g['name']}",'',
 f"- **Runtime arena:** {g['width']} W × {g['height']} clear H × {g['depth']} D; floor footprint {g['footprint']:,}. Public structural raft: {g['width']+40}×{g['depth']+40} = {fp:,}; the geological mass and service approach extend beyond this building footprint.",
 f"- **Built permanent components:** {counts.get(key,0)} Parts; active hazards and interior technical components are additional and exist only during a match.",
 f"- **Architectural identity:** {g['silhouette']}. Standard support columns are 7 Studs thick, service gallery is 12 wide; room openings and technical routes are generated rather than represented by particles.",
 f"- **Party range:** {g['minPlayers']}–{g['players']}; **trial limit:** {g['duration']}s plus preparation; **base win reward:** {g['reward']} coins + one associated trophy, +15 participation, +40 for the whole five-trial run.",
 f"- **Design objective:** {g['rules']}.",f"- **Defeat cause:** {g['death']}. Actual runtime qualification and limitations are specified below, not assumed from the name.",
 f"- **Implemented state machine:** {DETAILS[g['kind']]}",
 '- **Entry/exit:** engraved west-hall stop → public mountain arrival pad → assembly selection. Return pad leads to the central plaza. A live trial is entered by the assembled team, with separate return handling on completion.',
 '- **Lighting/audio/animation:** daylight-readable permanent complex; warm work luminaires in private interiors; stone/metal or specialized ice/brick material contrast. Shared score-state routing selects preparation/calm/danger/movement/impact/elimination/final/victory cues. Impact audio is spatial; original soundtrack cues require uploaded IDs (see AUDIO.md). Contact-derived procedural death poses are used, with the cause above.',
 '- **Structural vs visual:** raft/piers/walls/floors/platforms are collision geometry; inscriptions/light strips/particle accents are visual. Drive rails and housings explain movement paths; kinematic motion does not pretend the decorative housing physically powers a real constraint solver.','']
lines += ['## Known unfinished requirements — do not hide these','',
'- No actual Roblox Studio rendering, physics, live multiplayer replication, R6/R15 motor playback or live DataStore session test has been run in this cloud. The Luau API-double test is a logic regression test only.',
'- Every trial now has a named state machine, but the art uses a common construction kit and shared kinematic collision helpers. Bespoke captured animation sets and independently mixed soundscapes for each of fifty locations are not complete. The source-linked notes above distinguish puzzle rules from rigid-body simulation.',
'- Ten original WAV cues exist, but custom Roblox music cannot play until their asset IDs are uploaded/authorized and placed in Catalog.AudioAssets. No false asset IDs or unlicensed catalog audio are used.',
'- Profile session locking, rejoin recovery, production anti-exploit review, mobile layouts and measured streaming/LOD budgets remain release work. Terrain is built from collision landform Parts; this is not hand-sculpted voxel Terrain or a photorealistic asset pack.',
'- Consequently this is a substantially rebuilt playable development project and detailed construction ledger, **not a completed production implementation of every requirement in the brief**.','']
(ROOT/'docs/PROJECT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
(ROOT/'docs/mountains.json').write_text(json.dumps(records(),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Documented 50 trial contracts and exact museum/lobby areas')
